  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_008 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, transformer, weighted) is our best at 0.5729 acc but costs 6.61 GPU hrs, largely due to transformer aggregation. The RNA-only baseline (0.5191) confirms multimodal adds ~5% value. Question: Is the expensive transformer aggregation actually necessary, or does simple average pooling (avgpool) capture most of the multiprofile information at a fraction of the cost? This experiment (config_007) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_008 (transformer→avgpool, everything else identical), directly testing whether the ~4+ GPU hr premium of the transformer is justified. If avgpool matches or nearly matches 0.5729, we unlock much cheaper multimodal configs for the remaining 7 experiments, preserving budget for exploring image encoders and RNA encoders. If it falls short, we confirm transformer aggregation is critical and can confidently invest remaining budget in transformer-based variants. Expected cost: ~2–3 GPU hrs (roughly 40–50% of config_008), making it a high-information, low-cost experiment that reduces uncertainty about the most expensive architectural component before committing further budget."
}

